<title>USA: US banks free reserves $678 mln Oct 23 rvsd 2 wks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $678 mln Oct 23 rvsd 2 wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had revised free reserves of $678 million per day in the two weeks ended Oct 23 versus revised free reserves of $677 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $205 million against $275 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
